    "raw_public_english_response": "Proposal submitted and accepted. Summary of the outcome:\n\n**Submission receipt** — `normalization_applied: true`, raw contract valid, no conflicting explicit setting fields. The case-bound normalizer filled the explicit task-derived slot `settings.freq = true` (task kind `freq`); all other fields preserved as submitted.\n\n**Final blocked proposal** (`case_id: orca-b3lyp-d3zero-unsupported`, program `orca`, project `orca-b3lyp-d3zero-unsupported`):\n- **Readiness:** `blocked_unsupported_setting`\n- **Settings (source literals preserved):** functional `B3LYP-D3ZERO`, basis `def2-SVP`, freq `true`; no dispersion/grid/solvent/ECP fields claimed.\n- **Blocking rules:** `scientific_settings.v2.non_exhaustive_scope_unverified` (functional) and `scientific_settings.v2.validation_coverage_gap` (basis)\n- No native input authored, no command authored, no project written, no execution requested.\n\n**Basis for the block, from read-only V2 evidence only:**\n1. **Functional `B3LYP-D3ZERO`** — `matched_count: 0`, resolution `unknown_unverified`; no canonical candidate, `source_registered: false`. The compound string is not registry-supported; it was not reduced to plain B3LYP and was not claimed compiler-ready.\n2. **Basis `def2-SVP`** — matched entry `setting.orca.method_basis.9d4ad2a94a78c138096c` is loader/renderer-verified only (`deterministic_validator_enforced: false`, evidence ceiling `loader_renderer_verification_only`), so it is `blocked_validation_coverage`; its declared applicability rules (`ecp_applicability_required`, `request_element_coverage_required`) remain undischarged with no element data in scope.\n\nNo project candidate is eligible, and no execution path was opened.",
